# Sources used:
# - PAN M 360, Francos de Montreal, Malko a la scene Desjardins (opened 2026-10-20, text from Cult Nation): age 23, influences Josman, Laylow and Stromae, fashion and visual arts; summer 2023, 30 degrees, trio with Afro influences, co written and co produced by Willy Wonder and Hypnotic Beatz (Damso, SCH); MOTOMAMI most streamed song of his Spotify catalog within weeks; debut EP MAELSTROM a few months later; first Francophone artist named Breakthrough Artist by Amazon Music Canada; back to Paris spring 2024 with producers RayDaPrince, Lucci and Bloody; SAHARA four pack in July 2024 and Emotionnellement indisponible in fall 2024 with Chanceko on Parapluie.
# - Qobuz, 30 degrees album page (opened 2026-10-20): released 18 Aug 2023, Cult Nation, 3 tracks, TORNADE, MOTOMAMI, ONE LOVE; MOTOMAMI and ONE LOVE credits: Willy Wonder producer, Yannick Cabald composer, Hypnotic Beats producer, William Lareau composer, Malko Joseph-Lissade composer; TORNADE credits without Hypnotic.
# - Qobuz, MAELSTROM album page (opened 2026-10-20): released 1 Dec 2023, Cult Nation, Hip-Hop/Rap, 6 tracks, GOD COMPLEX, paradis, TRISTE ET CELEBRE, P3LE with Halo, le monde sur moi, lettre a maman; Hypnotic Beats producer on P3LE and lettre a maman.
# - Qobuz, SAHARA album page (opened 2026-10-20): released 19 Jul 2024, Cult Nation, 4 tracks, Aaliyah, Baby Push, Habanero, Mami Quiere; Hypnotic Beatz producer on Aaliyah, Baby Push and Mami Quiere, not on Habanero.
# - Qobuz, Emotionnellement indisponible album page (opened 2026-10-20): released 11 Oct 2024, Cult Nation, 6 tracks, Champagne, Club Story, title track, DNA, Parapluie with Chanceko as main artist alongside Malko, Le plus beau des diamants; Hypnotic Beatz producer on five of the six tracks, Club Story produced by RayDaPrince among others.
# - Qobuz, Malko discography page (opened 2026-10-20): the page merges many artists named Malko (492 albums listed); the Cult Nation line is identifiable by label and by the composer credit Malko Joseph-Lissade; same page lists earlier and later Cult Nation singles Spleen Amore (17 Nov 2021), Patience (Stripped) (21 Apr 2023), Danny Glover (22 Jan 2025) and Fashion Week (18 Jul 2025), plus NEEDA, Autoproducido, Bonsai Music and other labels that belong to other Malkos.
# - Atuvu, Premier Gala de l ADISQ 2025 winners (opened 2026-10-20): ceremony 5 Nov 2025 at MTELUS; Album of the Year R&B/Soul nominees ANJXLXE, Blynk, Malko for Emotionnellement indisponible, Naomi, Shah Frank; winner Shah Frank, Aura. Malko was a nominee, not the winner.
# Note: no opened source gives Malko a birthplace or a bouyon record. His link to this site is the Hypnotic Beatz production credit, the producer documented on this site as HYPNO. This profile states that link exactly and claims no bouyon title for him.

